A growable sequence of bytes with a final zero byte.

A final zero byte keeps every buffer ready for kernel calls.
Whitespace means space, tab, line feed, or carriage return.

Use alloc, core, and io.

A public record TcString has a data (a pointer to byte), a len (an unsigned number), and a cap (an unsigned number).

Publicly, to create an empty text, named str_new, giving TcString.
Let empty text be TcString.
Give back empty text.

Publicly, to create text from p (a pointer to byte) of length n (an unsigned number), named str_from_bytes, giving TcString.
Let s be TcString.
Let capacity be n plus 1 as an unsigned number.
Let allocated be allocate capacity bytes.
Update s so its len is n, its cap is capacity, and its data is allocated.
If n is positive, copy n bytes from p to s's data.
Set item n of s's data to 0.
Give back s.

Publicly, to append to s (a pointer to TcString) text p (a pointer to byte) of length n (an unsigned number), named str_push_bytes.
If n is zero, give back.
Let needed be s's len plus n plus 1.
If needed is more than s's cap.
Let new cap be s's cap times 2.
If new cap is less than needed, make new cap needed.
If new cap is less than 16, make new cap 16 as an unsigned number.
Let old cap be s's cap.
Let resized be resize memory at s's data from old cap to new cap.
Update s so its data is resized and its cap is new cap.
End the condition.
Copy n bytes from p to (s's data as an unsigned number plus s's len) as a pointer to byte.
Set s's len to s's len plus n.
Set item s's len of s's data to 0.

Publicly, to join a (a pointer to TcString) and b (a pointer to TcString), named str_concat, giving TcString.
Let joined be create text from a's data of length a's len.
Append to address of joined text b's data of length b's len.
Give back joined.

Publicly, to compare text a (a pointer to TcString) with text b (a pointer to TcString), named str_eq, giving a truth value.
Call this as "text <a> matches text <b>".
If a's len is not equal to b's len, give back false.
Let i start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while i is less than a's len.
If item i of a's data isn't equal to item i of b's data, give back false.
Add 1 to i.
End the loop.
Give back true.

Publicly, to find the length of s (a pointer to TcString), named str_len, giving an unsigned number.
Give back s's len.

Publicly, to copy text s (a pointer to TcString), named str_clone, giving TcString.
Call this as "copy text <s>".
Let copied be create text from s's data of length s's len.
Give back copied.

Publicly, to clear text s (a pointer to TcString), named str_clear.
Call this as "clear text <s>".
Set s's len to 0 as an unsigned number.
If s's data is not empty, set item 0 of s's data to 0.

Publicly, to release text s (a pointer to TcString), named str_free.
If s's data is not empty, release memory at s's data.
Update s so its data is no address, its len is 0 as an unsigned number, and its cap is 0 as an unsigned number.

Publicly, to show s (a pointer to TcString), named show_str.
Say s.

Publicly, to print s (a pointer to TcString), named print_synonym_str.
Say s.

Publicly, to display s (a pointer to TcString), named display_str.
Say s.

Publicly, to say s (a pointer to TcString), named print_str.
If s's len is positive, ask Linux kernel 1 with 1, s's data, and s's len.
Ask Linux kernel 1 with 1, "\n", and 1.

Publicly, to check whether text s (a pointer to TcString) starts with prefix (a pointer to TcString), named str_starts_with, giving a truth value.
Call this as "text <s> starts with <prefix>".
If prefix's len is more than s's len, give back false.
Let i start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while i is less than prefix's len.
If item i of s's data isn't equal to item i of prefix's data, give back false.
Add 1 to i.
End the loop.
Give back true.

Publicly, to check whether text s (a pointer to TcString) ends with suffix (a pointer to TcString), named str_ends_with, giving a truth value.
Call this as "text <s> ends with <suffix>".
If suffix's len is more than s's len, give back false.
Let offset be s's len minus suffix's len.
Let i start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while i is less than suffix's len.
If item (offset plus i) of s's data isn't equal to item i of suffix's data, give back false.
Add 1 to i.
End the loop.
Give back true.

Publicly, to check whether text s (a pointer to TcString) contains needle (a pointer to TcString), named str_contains, giving a truth value.
Call this as "text <s> contains <needle>".
If needle's len is zero, give back true.
If needle's len is more than s's len, give back false.
Let offset start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while offset plus needle's len is at most s's len.
Let i start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Let matched be true.
Repeat while i is less than needle's len.
If item (offset plus i) of s's data isn't equal to item i of needle's data, set matched to false, break.
Add 1 to i.
End the loop.
If matched, give back true.
Add 1 to offset.
End the loop.
Give back false.

Publicly, to trim text s (a pointer to TcString), named str_trim, giving TcString.
Call this as "trim text <s>".
If s's len is zero, give back create an empty text.
Let left start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while left is less than s's len.
If item left of s's data is 32 or item left of s's data is 9 or item left of s's data is 10 or item left of s's data is 13, add 1 to left, otherwise break.
End the loop.
If left equals s's len, give back create an empty text.
Let right be s's len.
Repeat while right is more than left.
If item (right minus 1) of s's data is 32 or item (right minus 1) of s's data is 9 or item (right minus 1) of s's data is 10 or item (right minus 1) of s's data is 13, subtract 1 from right, otherwise break.
End the loop.
Give back create text from (s's data as an unsigned number plus left) as a pointer to byte of length (right minus left).

Publicly, to trim p (a pointer to byte) of length n (an unsigned number), named str_trim_bytes, giving TcString.
Let s be create text from p of length n.
Give back trim text address of s.

Publicly, to parse a whole number from text s (a pointer to TcString), named str_parse_i64, giving Result of whole number and whole number.
Call this as "parse whole number from <s>".
Let answer be Result of whole number and whole number.
Set answer's is_ok to false.
Set answer's err_val to 1.
If s's len is zero, give back answer.
Let position start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while position is less than s's len.
If item position of s's data is 32 or item position of s's data is 9 or item position of s's data is 10 or item position of s's data is 13, add 1 to position, otherwise break.
End the loop.
If position equals s's len, give back answer.
Let negative be false.
If item position of s's data is 45, set negative to true, add 1 to position.
If position is less than s's len and item position of s's data is 43, add 1 to position.
If position equals s's len, give back answer.
Let value start at 0.
Let digits start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while position is less than s's len.
Let b be item position of s's data.
If b is less than 48 or b is more than 57, break.
Set value to value times 10 plus (b as a whole number) minus 48.
Add 1 to position.
Add 1 to digits.
End the loop.
If digits is zero, give back answer.
Repeat while position is less than s's len.
If item position of s's data is 32 or item position of s's data is 9 or item position of s's data is 10 or item position of s's data is 13, add 1 to position, otherwise give back answer.
End the loop.
If negative, set value to 0 minus value.
Set answer's is_ok to true.
Set answer's ok_val to value.
Give back answer.

Publicly, to format n (a whole number) as whole number text, named str_from_i64, giving TcString.
Call this as "format whole number <n> as text".
Let buffer be block of 32 byte.
Let text length be format n into address of item 0 of buffer.
Give back create text from address of item 0 of buffer of length text length.

Publicly, to append text given target as a pointer to TcString, source as a pointer to TcString, named str_append_text.
If source's len is zero, give back.
Append to target text source's data of length source's len.

Publicly, to append a byte given target as a pointer to TcString, value as a byte, named str_append_byte.
Let buffer be block of 1 byte.
Set item 0 of buffer to value.
Append to target text address of item 0 of buffer of length 1.

Publicly, to slice given source as a pointer to byte, len as an unsigned number, start as a whole number, finish as a whole number, named str_slice, giving TcString.
If start is less than 0, make start 0 as a whole number.
If finish is more than len as a whole number, make finish len as a whole number.
If finish is at most start, give back create an empty text.
Let from be start as an unsigned number.
Let count be (finish - start) as an unsigned number.
Give back create text from (source as an unsigned number plus from) as a pointer to byte of length count.

Publicly, to compare bytes primary (a pointer to byte) of length counta (an unsigned number) with bytes secondary (a pointer to byte) of length countb (an unsigned number), named str_equal_bytes, giving a truth value.
If counta is not countb, give back false.
Let position start at 0 as an unsigned number.
Repeat while position is less than counta.
If item position of primary is not item position of secondary, give back false.
Add 1 to position.
End the loop.
Give back true.
